<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">First Seminole War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1817–1818</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The First Seminole War was a conflict of 1817 to 1818 in which American forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andrew-jackson">Andrew Jackson</a> invaded Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a> against the Seminole and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-seminoles">Black Seminoles</a>. Jackson burned towns, seized the Spanish posts of St. Marks and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pensacola">Pensacola</a> and executed two British traders. The campaign helped persuade <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> to cede Florida to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> in the Adams-Onís Treaty of 1819.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-seminole-war.jpg" alt="First Seminole War" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: U.S. Marine Corps · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seminole_War_in_Everglades.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
